meson: link libregex when there is one (QNX)

QNX keeps the POSIX regex functions (regcomp, regexec, regerror, regfree)
in libregex, not in libc; foot (its configuration and URL mode) fails to
link with "undefined reference to regcomp". Link libregex where the
library exists (an optional find_library, as for stdthreads).

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -137,6 +137,8 @@
 math = cc.find_library('m')
 threads = [dependency('threads'), cc.find_library('stdthreads', required: false)]
 libepoll = dependency('epoll-shim', required: false)
+# regcomp()/regexec(): in libregex on QNX, not in libc
+libregex = cc.find_library('regex', required: false)
 pixman = dependency('pixman-1')
 wayland_protocols = dependency('wayland-protocols', version: '>=1.41',
                                fallback: 'wayland-protocols',
@@ -293,7 +295,7 @@
     'pgo',
     'pgo/pgo.c',
     wl_proto_src + wl_proto_headers,
-    dependencies: [math, threads, libepoll, pixman, wayland_client, xkb, utf8proc, fcft, tllist],
+    dependencies: [math, threads, libepoll, libregex, pixman, wayland_client, xkb, utf8proc, fcft, tllist],
     link_with: pgolib,
   )
 endif
@@ -327,7 +329,7 @@
   'wayland.c', 'wayland.h', 'shm-formats.h',
   'xkbcommon-vmod.h',
   srgb_funcs, wl_proto_src + wl_proto_headers, version,
-  dependencies: [math, threads, libepoll, pixman, wayland_client, wayland_cursor, xkb, fontconfig, utf8proc,
+  dependencies: [math, threads, libepoll, libregex, pixman, wayland_client, wayland_cursor, xkb, fontconfig, utf8proc,
                  tllist, fcft],
   link_with: pgolib,
   install: true)
